      "message": "Classify quadratic biform ranks and exclude rank 13 in the 3-by-3 block (#218)\n\nThis gives an effective rank formula for arbitrary quadratic biforms and\nrestricts its two polynomial kernel indices. For a=b=3, the nonzero\nfifteen-by-fifteen biform block has exactly the ranks {9,12,14,15} over\nevery field. Rank13 is excluded, and universal witnesses attain the four\nlisted values. More generally, for every balanced a=b>=3 quadratic-z\nfamily, ranks lie in {a\u00b2,a\u00b2+a,a\u00b2+2a\u22121,a\u00b2+2a}; attainment of all four\nvalues is not asserted at larger sizes.\n\nAfter dividing the common coefficient gcd, let D be the largest\nremaining degree. The indices sum to aD, their first nonzero\ncoefficient-kernel degree recovers both, and the source rank is ab +\nmin(b,mu1) + min(b,mu2). A minimum recurrence vector either has Hankel\nrank two and degree at least ceil((a-1)D/2), or comes from a rational\nroot of height h and degree (a+1)h. The proof covers zero endpoints,\ncommon factors, D=0 and characteristic two.\n\nClaims: AI-QUADRATIC-KERNEL-INDICES-001 and\nAI-QUADRATIC-INDEX-DICHOTOMY-002, both proof-written-unreviewed. The\nprior general biform kernel-bundle identity and special-family formulas\nretain their credit. External inputs: Schoemann\u2013Wiedmann\narXiv:1712.03056v1, Theorem2.1; De Teran\u2013Dopico\u2013Mackey MIMS\nEPrint2013.47 (August22 2013), Theorem6.5. Exact versions, hypotheses\nand source hashes are in sources.json.\n\nValidation at f00613b:\n- 2,050 complete source-matrix comparisons over Q,F2,F3,F5, including\nall nonzero F2 triples for a=2,3.\n- 567 positive-degree minimum vectors inspected, with 1,696 direct\nHankel kernel-nullity checks including named controls.\n- Universal rank witnesses; the rank15 witness has an exact integer\ndeterminant of \u22121 and seven verified unit-determinant blocks.\n- All10 focused tests pass against an immutable export of the committed\nfiles and ordinary on-disk report.\n- Repository consistency18 tests, integrated top-coefficient3 tests and\nintegrated paired-window6 tests pass.\n- All five frozen archive replays pass; ten source files verified.\n- Required hosted regression suite completed on\n`f00613b057cc4437fad4d10e22f1b6c8cc891872`: all eight Python 3.10/3.14\ngroups and archive replay passed, and aggregate `CI` succeeded ([run\n40004703350](https://github.com/1337isnot1337/matrix-mult-bounds/actions/runs/40004703350)).\nThe focused checks above are the recorded local coverage.\n\nReproduction: python -m unittest discover -s tests -p\ntest_quadratic_kernel_indices.py -v; python -m unittest discover -s\ntests -v; python tools/replay.py.\n\nThis classifies biform-block ranks in the stated scope, not every full\ncyclic-tensor slice. No source-space cap, compatible three-leg maps,\ndegeneration, independent mathematical review, formalization or exponent\nimprovement is claimed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cinna Davis <1337isnot1337@users.noreply.github.com>",
