    "title": "Classify quadratic biform ranks and exclude rank 13 in the 3-by-3 block",
    "user": {
      "login": "1337isnot1337",
      "id": 164028474,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOCcbgOg",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/164028474?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1337isnot1337",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1337isnot1337",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1337isnot1337/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1337isnot1337/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1337isnot1337/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1337isnot1337/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1337isnot1337/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1337isnot1337/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1337isnot1337/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1337isnot1337/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1337isnot1337/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "This gives an effective rank formula for arbitrary quadratic biforms and restricts its two polynomial kernel indices. For a=b=3, the nonzero fifteen-by-fifteen biform block has exactly the ranks {9,12,14,15} over every field. Rank13 is excluded, and universal witnesses attain the four listed values. More generally, for every balanced a=b>=3 quadratic-z family, ranks lie in {a\u00b2,a\u00b2+a,a\u00b2+2a\u22121,a\u00b2+2a}; attainment of all four values is not asserted at larger sizes.\n\nAfter dividing the common coefficient gcd, let D be the largest remaining degree. The indices sum to aD, their first nonzero coefficient-kernel degree recovers both, and the source rank is ab + min(b,mu1) + min(b,mu2). A minimum recurrence vector either has Hankel rank two and degree at least ceil((a-1)D/2), or comes from a rational root of height h and degree (a+1)h. The proof covers zero endpoints, common factors, D=0 and characteristic two.\n\nClaims: AI-QUADRATIC-KERNEL-INDICES-001 and AI-QUADRATIC-INDEX-DICHOTOMY-002, both proof-written-unreviewed. The prior general biform kernel-bundle identity and special-family formulas retain their credit. External inputs: Schoemann\u2013Wiedmann arXiv:1712.03056v1, Theorem2.1; De Teran\u2013Dopico\u2013Mackey MIMS EPrint2013.47 (August22 2013), Theorem6.5. Exact versions, hypotheses and source hashes are in sources.json.\n\nValidation at f00613b:\n- 2,050 complete source-matrix comparisons over Q,F2,F3,F5, including all nonzero F2 triples for a=2,3.\n- 567 positive-degree minimum vectors inspected, with 1,696 direct Hankel kernel-nullity checks including named controls.\n- Universal rank witnesses; the rank15 witness has an exact integer determinant of \u22121 and seven verified unit-determinant blocks.\n- All10 focused tests pass against an immutable export of the committed files and ordinary on-disk report.\n- Repository consistency18 tests, integrated top-coefficient3 tests and integrated paired-window6 tests pass.\n- All five frozen archive replays pass; ten source files verified.\n- Required hosted regression suite completed on `f00613b057cc4437fad4d10e22f1b6c8cc891872`: all eight Python 3.10/3.14 groups and archive replay passed, and aggregate `CI` succeeded ([run 40004703350](https://github.com/1337isnot1337/matrix-mult-bounds/actions/runs/40004703350)). The focused checks above are the recorded local coverage.\n\nReproduction: python -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_quadratic_kernel_indices.py -v; python -m unittest discover -s tests -v; python tools/replay.py.\n\nThis classifies biform-block ranks in the stated scope, not every full cyclic-tensor slice. No source-space cap, compatible three-leg maps, degeneration, independent mathematical review, formalization or exponent improvement is claimed.",
